--TEST--
a `#[Json\Derive]` property typed as a union of two kinds, `string|int` or two classes, has no JSON form, and the help names `mixed` and a set of allowed values — `rule:core-classes/derive-property-list`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/core-json-derive-and-core-json-field-a-class-with-a-json-codec
#[Core\Json\Derive]
class A {
    public function constructor(public int $n) {}
}

#[Core\Json\Derive]
class B {
    public function constructor(public string $s) {}
}

#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Holder {
    public function constructor(public string|int $id, public A|B $item) {}
}
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0756]: %s$id%s
%A
   = help: %smixed%sset of allowed values%s
%A
error[E0756]: %s$item%s
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
